  "articleBody": "Tiling a wall seems straightforward, but a few common missteps can really derail your project. One major mistake is working on a dirty or uneven wall. If your substrate isn't clean and level, your tiles won't lay flat, leading to an uneven finish and potential cracking down the line. Another pitfall is applying too much adhesive at once. This causes it to skin over before you can set the tiles, meaning they won't bond properly. You should only spread enough adhesive that you can cover with tile within 10-15 minutes. Also, don't forget to clean up excess adhesive immediately! Once it hardens, it's a real pain to remove. Finally, an unbalanced layout, where you end up with tiny slivers of tile at the edges, can really detract from the overall look. HH Remodeling LLC always takes the time to plan the layout, ensuring a professional, balanced aesthetic. When in doubt, or if you're tackling a complex design, getting expert help can save you from costly re-dos.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}